# issue-number.conf — OPT-IN list for git-hooks/pre-push check (1b). Copy this file to
# hooks/issue-number.conf (next to the other hook conf files) and list one repo per line as
# owner/name. A push to refs/heads/main of a listed repo is then refused when any commit it
# adds changes a path outside docs/** and the root *.md files (CLAUDE.md counts as outside)
# without an issue number (#<N>, N >= 1) in its message. No conf file, or a repo not listed
# here: the check never runs. Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored; case does not
# matter. The repo is recognised by the push TARGET (the last two parts of its URL, without a
# trailing / or .git), not by the folder you push from.
# Deliberate exception for one push: ISSUE_OK=1 git push ... (one line in the override ledger).
#
# example-owner/example-repo
